| !Run for !PCSX - PCSX ReARMed, the PlayStation emulator, for RISC OS.
| Built with GCCSDK GCC 10.2 (arm-riscos-gnueabihf), statically linked
| and converted to an Absolute (AIF) file, so !SharedLibs isn't needed.
| The desktop frontend is native: no SDL.

Set PCSX$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <PCSX$Dir>.!Sprites

RMEnsure UtilityModule 5.00 Error PCSX needs RISC OS 5.

| --- C library ------------------------------------------------------
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error PCSX needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error PCSX needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.

| --- Sound ------------------------------------------------------------
| Sound goes through SharedSoundBuffer, StreamManager and SharedSound
| (in !System), mixed with other programs' sound. SharedSound is part of
| RISC OS; SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager are in ssb.zip from
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html. Without them
| games run silently (paced by the clock instead of the sound).
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer

| --- Joysticks --------------------------------------------------------
| USB game pads work through !USBJoystick (Richard Walker's USBJoystick
| module, 0.23 or later): run it before PCSX, or put it in your boot
| sequence. Pads plugged in later are found within a second.

| --- Your files -------------------------------------------------------
| BIOS images (optional), memory cards, save states, covers and per-game
| settings live in <Choices$Write>.PCSX: bios, saves, states, covers,
| games; Library is the games library. Choices is a text file of
| settings (the icon bar menu's Choices... opens it).
IfThere <Choices$Write>.PCSX Then Else CDir <Choices$Write>.PCSX
IfThere <Choices$Write>.PCSX.bios Then Else CDir <Choices$Write>.PCSX.bios
IfThere <Choices$Write>.PCSX.covers Then Else CDir <Choices$Write>.PCSX.covers
IfThere <Choices$Write>.PCSX.games Then Else CDir <Choices$Write>.PCSX.games
IfThere <Choices$Write>.PCSX.Choices Then Else Copy <PCSX$Dir>.Resources.UserChoices <Choices$Write>.PCSX.Choices ~C~V

| --- Logging ----------------------------------------------------------
| For a log in <Wimp$ScrapDir>.pcsxlog (useful when reporting a
| problem), keep the next line; put a | in front of it for no log.
Set PCSX$LogOn 1
Unset PCSX$Log
If "<PCSX$LogOn>"<>"" Then Set PCSX$Log /|<Wimp$ScrapDir>/pcsxlog
Unset PCSX$LogOn

| --- Memory -----------------------------------------------------------
| The program and the dynamic recompiler's 16 MB code cache are in the
| WimpSlot; the C heap goes in a dynamic area ("PCSX Heap"), which grows
| past 100 MB only to unpack a 7z made with a big dictionary.
WimpSlot -min 28000K -max 28000K

Run <PCSX$Dir>.!RunImage %*0
